  "about": "More or less for all wine types winemaking stages are similar. It starts from maturing grapes on wine fields, collecting them when they are ready, transportation to a winery, crushing, pressing juice, fermentation process, refining the taste of wine, and then leaving for aging at stable environmental conditions. When wine is ready-tasting, bottled, and brought to the customer. The scale of the wine factory is disproportionate to the small village of Boyuk-Gamya, but creating an interior human-scale atmosphere can help bring relationships between the village and the factory back.",
